-- title:
--   Degree ℓ over the Igusa field when ℓ ∣ M
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $\kappa$ a field of characteristic $p$, and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$. Let $w$ be an integral weight-one form of level $M$ over $\kappa$, that is: a modular form of weight $1$ for $\Gamma_1(M)$ (viewed inside $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$), together with a power series over $\mathbb{Z}$ whose image under $\mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{C}$ is the $q$-expansion of that form, and subject to the condition that the Laurent series over $\kappa$ obtained by reducing this integral series is nonzero. Let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \neq p$ and $\ell \mid M$. Write $\mathrm{Ig}$ for the intermediate field of $\kappa((q))$ over $\kappa$ generated by the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(M)$ over $\kappa$ together with the inverse of the reduced series of $w$. Then the $\mathrm{Ig}$-vector space $\mathrm{Ig}\bigl(\bar j(q^{M\ell})\bigr)$, the intermediate field of $\kappa((q))$ over $\mathrm{Ig}$ generated by the single element $\bar j(q^{M\ell})$ (the $q$-expansion of $j$ with coefficients reduced into $\kappa$, with $q$ replaced by $q^{M\ell}$), has finite rank exactly $\ell$.
--
--   This is the branch $\ell \mid M$ of the computation of the degree of the level-raising extension obtained by adjoining $\bar j(q^{M\ell})$ to the Igusa function field of level $M$ in characteristic $p$. Together with the complementary branch $\ell \nmid M$ it feeds the combined degree statement [`ModularCurve.finrank_adjoin_jqNModC_igusaFunctionFieldX1C_eq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.finrank_adjoin_jqNModC_igusaFunctionFieldX1C_eq).
